{"name":"Hello Darkness My Old Friend","hex":"#802280","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hello","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["A greeting (salutation) said when meeting someone or acknowledging someone’s arrival or presence.","A greeting used when answering the telephone."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["\"Hello!\" or an equivalent greeting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hello"},{"term":"darkness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dark; lack of light; the absolute or comparative absence of light.","The state or quality of reflecting little light, of tending to a blackish or brownish color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darkness"},{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Sound of Silence","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Sound of Silence\" is a song by the American folk rock duo Simon & Garfunkel, written by Paul Simon. The duo's studio audition of the song led to a record deal with Columbia Records, and the original acoustic version was recorded in March 1964 at Columbia's 7th Avenue Recording Studios in New York City for their debut album, Wednesday Morning, 3 A.M., released that October to disappointing sales. An overdubbed electric remix was released the following year and went to number one on the Billboard singles chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/The_Sounds_of_Silence_by_Simon_and_Garfunkel_US_vinyl.png/330px-The_Sounds_of_Silence_by_Simon_and_Garfunkel_US_vinyl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sound_of_Silence","wikidata":"Q922139"},{"title":"My Old Friend","blocks":[{"text":"\"My Old Friend\" is a song written by Craig Wiseman and Steve McEwan, and recorded by American country music artist Tim McGraw. It was released in September 2005 as the fifth and final single from his album Live Like You Were Dying. It peaked at number 6 on the country music charts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d3/Tim_McGraw_-_My_Old_Friend_cover.png/330px-Tim_McGraw_-_My_Old_Friend_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Old_Friend","wikidata":"Q6946181"},{"title":"Hello","blocks":[{"text":"Hello is a salutation or greeting in the English language. It is first attested in writing from 1826."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg/330px-TelephoneHelloNellie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hello","wikidata":"Q98815142"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness","wikidata":"Q204170"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg/500px-Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg/500px-Paul_Simon_in_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paul Simon, the song's composer, c. 1966","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaul_Simon_in_1966.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w